{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they were gathered.</b> They were accustomed to gather, because the stone was large." "<b>And they rolled.</b> And they roll. Its Targum: וּמְגַנְדְּרִין. Every present-tense form changes to be expressed in the future tense and in the past tense, because anything that is continual has already been and is destined to be." "<b>And they returned.</b> Its Targum: וּמְתִיבִין."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:02.569047336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}